==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-first base.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-NaomiAmethyst-first base.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|singulare tantum|baseball}} The base after home plate in a counter-clockwise path around a baseball [[infield]].
#: {{ux|en|The [[runner]] took his [[lead]] off '''first base'''.}}
# {{lb|en|singulare tantum|by extension}} Completion of the first phase of an activity.
# {{lb|en|singulare tantum|US|colloquial}} [[kissing|Kissing]], regarded as the first phase of a sexual relationship.
#:{{ux|en|I got to '''first base''' with Danny, and hope to get him naked this weekend.}}
#* {{RQ:Salinger Catcher|page=104|passage=Every time I got to the part about her out with Stradlater in that damn Ed Banky's car, it almost drove me crazy. I knew she wouldn’t let him get to '''first base''' with her, but it drove me crazy anyway.}}
# {{lb|en|blackjack}} The betting spot located immediately to the left of the dealer, which is first to receive cards and first to act.

